  </div>

  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers two things operated by Matt Donders: the <strong>Quiz Parade</strong> app for
    iPhone, and the <strong>Quiz Parade Publisher</strong>, a private server-side tool that uploads
    Quiz Parade's daily videos to its own YouTube channel.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>No personal information.</strong> Quiz Parade does not ask you to sign up or sign in, and
    does not collect your name, email address, contacts, location, photos, or any identifier for you
    or your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app sends anonymous events such as "quiz started", "quiz completed", "Daily Quiz completed",
    and whether a question pack downloaded successfully. Each event contains only the event name, the
    app version, the pack it relates to, and a number such as a score or a count. Events are not linked to
    each other, to a device, or to a person, and they never include your individual answers.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the app crashes, iOS provides a crash summary through Apple's MetricKit framework. Quiz Parade
    sends only the type of crash and the app version: no stack traces, device identifiers, or
    personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Your scores, statistics, settings and downloaded question packs are stored on your
    device. They are not uploaded. Deleting the app removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloaded Content</h2>
  <p>
    New question packs and the Daily Quiz are downloaded from <code>quizparade.mattdonders.com</code>,
    which is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any website, Cloudflare necessarily processes your device's IP
    address to deliver the request. Quiz Parade does not store IP addresses or use them to identify
    you.
  </p>

  <h2>Game Center</h2>
  <p>
    Leaderboards use Apple Game Center and are optional. If you are signed in to Game Center, your
    score is submitted to Apple under your Game Center profile. That data is handled by Apple under
    Apple's privacy policy. Quiz Parade does not receive your Apple Account details.
  </p>

  <h2>Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    The daily reminder is off by default. If you turn it on, the reminder is scheduled on your device
    by iOS. No push service or server is involved.
  </p>

  <h2>Tracking, Advertising, and Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Quiz Parade has no advertising, does not track you across apps or websites, contains no
    third-party analytics or advertising SDKs, and has no in-app purchases. We do not sell or share
    any data.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Quiz Parade is family-friendly trivia intended for grown-ups and kids to enjoy together. It does
    not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13, because it
    collects no personal information at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Quiz Parade Publisher and Google User Data</h2>
  <p>
    The Quiz Parade Publisher is a private automation tool used only by its owner. It is not offered
    to the public and no other users sign in to it. It uses Google OAuth to access the owner's own
    Quiz Parade YouTube channel with two permissions:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>youtube.upload</code>: to upload and schedule Quiz Parade's daily videos.</li>
    <li><code>youtube.readonly</code>: to confirm which channel it is connected to and to check the
      processing and publishing status of the videos it uploaded.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    OAuth tokens are stored on a private server with restricted access and are used only for these
    purposes. They are never shared with third parties, placed in a public repository, or used for
    advertising. No data from any other person's Google account is accessed. Access can be revoked at
    any time from
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account permissions</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Publisher's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. Uploaded videos are subject to the
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Terms of Service</a>
    and the
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>Any changes to this policy will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Quiz%20Parade%20Privacy">matt@mattdonders.com</a>.
  </p>
